  "articles": [
    {
      "id": "r20261114-a01",
      "title": "Grandma's Kitchen",
      "level": "Dasar",
      "min": 2,
      "body": [
        "Every Saturday, Nia goes to her grandmother's house. Her grandmother loves to cook, and her kitchen always smells wonderful. Today they are making klepon, small green rice cakes with sweet palm sugar inside.",
        "First, Grandma shows Nia how to mix rice flour with water and pandan juice. Nia rolls the dough into little balls and puts a piece of palm sugar in each one. Then they boil the balls in hot water. When the klepon float to the top, they are ready.",
        "Grandma rolls the klepon in fresh coconut. Nia takes her first bite, and warm sugar fills her mouth. \"Practice makes perfect,\" Grandma says with a smile. Nia already wants to come back next Saturday."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "grandmother": "nenek",
        "smells": "berbau",
        "rice flour": "tepung beras",
        "palm sugar": "gula aren",
        "dough": "adonan",
        "boil": "merebus",
        "float to the top": "mengapung ke atas",
        "coconut": "kelapa",
        "bite": "gigitan"
      },
