    {
      "id": "r20261114-a02",
      "title": "Slow Travel: Enjoying the Journey",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "For many travelers, a holiday used to mean visiting ten cities in seven days. They rushed from one famous place to another, took a quick photo, and moved on. Today, more and more people are choosing a different style: slow travel.",
        "Slow travel means spending more time in fewer places. Instead of changing hotels every night, a slow traveler might stay two weeks in a small town. They shop at the local market, learn a few words of the language, and find a favorite cafe. The goal is not to see everything, but to understand something.",
        "This way of traveling is often cheaper and less stressful. It is also kinder to the environment, because fewer flights and car rides mean less pollution. Most importantly, many slow travelers say their memories feel deeper and more personal. When you slow down, a place stops being a photo and becomes a story."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "rushed": "bergegas",
        "instead of": "alih-alih",
        "goal": "tujuan",
        "cheaper": "lebih murah",
        "stressful": "membuat stres",
        "environment": "lingkungan",
        "pollution": "polusi",
        "deeper": "lebih mendalam"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "What is the main idea of slow travel?",
